Major Language & JVM Features
1. Primitive Types in Patterns, instanceof, and switch

You can now use primitive types directly in pattern matching.

switch (obj) {
    case int i -> System.out.println("Integer: " + i);
    case double d -> System.out.println("Double: " + d);
    default -> System.out.println("Other");
}

Benefits:

More consistent pattern matching
Reduces boxing/unboxing overhead
2. Flexible Constructor Bodies

Statements can appear before constructor delegation (this(...) or super(...)).

Before:

public Person(String name) {
    super(name);   // had to be first
}

Now:

public Person(String name) {
    validate(name);
    super(name);
}

Benefits:

Cleaner validation and setup logic
Easier constructor refactoring
3. Compact Source Files and Instance Main Methods

Simplifies beginner programs.

void main() {
    System.out.println("Hello, Java 25!");
}

No class declaration is required for simple programs.

⚡ Performance & JVM Improvements
4. Stable Values API (Preview)

Provides safe, lazy initialization without complex synchronization.

StableValue<String> config =
    StableValue.of(() -> loadConfig());

Useful for:

Caches
Singletons
Expensive initialization
5. Ahead-of-Time Class Loading & Linking

Improves startup performance by preparing classes before execution.

Benefits:

Faster application startup
Better cloud/container performance
6. Generational Shenandoah GC

Adds a generational mode to the Shenandoah garbage collector.

Advantages:

Lower pause times
Better throughput
More efficient memory management
🧵 Concurrency Enhancements
7. Structured Concurrency (Preview Updates)

Improves management of related concurrent tasks.

try (var scope = new StructuredTaskScope.ShutdownOnFailure()) {
    var user = scope.fork(() -> fetchUser());
    var orders = scope.fork(() -> fetchOrders());

    scope.join();
    scope.throwIfFailed();

    return new Result(user.get(), orders.get());
}

Benefits:

Cleaner parallel code
Better error propagation
Easier cancellation handling
8. Scoped Values Improvements

An alternative to ThreadLocal for virtual threads.

static final ScopedValue<String> USER = ScopedValue.newInstance();

ScopedValue.where(USER, "Alice")
           .run(() -> processRequest());

Works especially well with virtual threads.

